                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I definitely recommend this game, especially in the way I got it, via a bundle. At it's Steam price of $4.99 it's slightly harder to recommend, but still a thumbs up.\n\nThe game overall is well polished, controls are great, controller support is flawless, and visually the levels and menus are pleasing. There are many options including changing the camera view, so if you think you might get dizzy that's easily solved in the game. It only took me two hours to complete the game and get all achievements, and this is how I played it: I didn't speed run, but I didn't attempt to get 5 starts on every map. I rescued almost every ball from each cage, and averaged 4 stars per level. At that rate, as well as only using \"spikeball\" powerups, it took me two hours.\n\nHere are the cons:\nThe level does not reset if you die/fall off the edge. This makes boss fights and just levels in general much easier. This may or may not have been intended, but i think it would have been better with level resets: reset the level to the stage when you hit the checkpoint.\nPowerups essentially make every level extremely simple. You can almost always cheat through a level using a few powerups, but I chose not to do this so I could actually experience the game.\nOverall it's a quite easy. This makes it nice and relaxing, especially when compared to a lot of games whose main draw is \"extremely difficult\" to beat. However, if you fixed the above two items, it would still be average difficulty and relaxing.\n\nI enjoyed my time playing Mazement and may come back to it in the future to grab some more stars. I would suggest you buy it on sale or from a bundle (mine was on Indiegala), but if you take your time and don't cheat your way through levels, anything under $3 is worth it.\n\nMy final note: the story made me cry.\nThat's a joke btw.\nThe story was really bad. It didn't need to be good, but there truly was minimal effort put into it.\n\nIf you think you'd like this game, buy it. If you're hesitant, perhaps you should wait.\n\n6.5/10",
